Stop gyp from rewriting the value part of a name=value argument on Windows

QuoteForRspFile() in msvs_emulation.py guesses which arguments are paths and runs
os.path.normpath() over them, because MSVC does not like foo/../bar. The guess is
"the argument contains a slash", so an argument that merely contains a path is
normalized as a whole. V8's inspector generator is called that way:

    --config_value protocol.path=../../deps/v8/include/js_protocol.pdl

normpath reads "protocol.path=.." as a directory, the ".." after it cancels it, and
what reaches the .rsp file is

    "--config_value" "deps/v8/include/js_protocol.pdl"

code_generator.py then parses the config file, finds no path entry in it and stops:

    AttributeError: 'X' object has no attribute 'path'
    FAILED: gen/inspector-generated-output-root/src/inspector/protocol/Forward.h ...

That is the first action after ICU in a Windows build (ninja 1130/4414). Only the
Windows flavour is affected: QuoteForRspFile is used for the .rsp files that gyp's
Windows ninja rules run through. Linux and macOS pass the argument as it is.

Normalizing only what follows the first "=" fixes it without changing any other
argument: text before an "=" is not a path spelling, and options that do carry a
path after "=" (MSVC's /Foout/..., -DFOO=/a/b/../c) still get their paths
normalized.

Verified on Linux by generating the ninja files with the Windows flavour
(./configure --ninja --dest-os=win ..., dummy Visual Studio through
GYP_MSVS_OVERRIDE_PATH, -G ninja_use_custom_environment_files=1), in
obj/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8_inspector_headers.ninja:

    before: "--config_value" "deps/v8/include/js_protocol.pdl"
    after:  "--config_value" "protocol.path=../../deps/v8/include/js_protocol.pdl"

--- a/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/msvs_emulation.py
+++ b/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/msvs_emulation.py
@@ -32,7 +32,18 @@
 
     # Use a heuristic to try to find args that are paths, and normalize them
     if arg.find("/") > 0 or arg.count("/") > 1:
-        arg = os.path.normpath(arg)
+        # GodotJS: for a name=value argument, normalize only the value. Running
+        # normpath over the whole argument treats "protocol.path=.." as a
+        # directory, which the following ".." cancels, so V8's inspector
+        # --config_value protocol.path=../../include/js_protocol.pdl came out as
+        # ../../include/... with the "protocol.path=" gone (and then the code
+        # generator fails with "'X' object has no attribute 'path'").
+        eq = arg.find("=")
+        slash = arg.find("/")
+        if 0 < eq < slash:
+            arg = arg[: eq + 1] + os.path.normpath(arg[eq + 1 :])
+        else:
+            arg = os.path.normpath(arg)
 
     # For a literal quote, CommandLineToArgvW requires 2n+1 backslashes
     # preceding it, and results in n backslashes + the quote. So we substitute
     in 2* what we match, +1 more, plus the quote.
